e":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.7.2 and 4.8-dev4\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev4 - Arch Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Fri, 21 Aug 2026 22:18:59 +0000 on Wayland - Wayland display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors (3840x2160 @ 240.00 Hz, 2880x1800 @ 120.00 Hz) - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Laptop GPU - Intel(R) Core(TM) Ultra 9 185H (22 threads) - 30.73 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nI have a game that released on GOG. GOG only supports Windows and Mac currently. In the [GDExtension](https://github.com/Blobfish-Games/godot-gog) to integrate the SDK, I only compiled for these platforms. However, when editing the project on Linux, the editor freezes every time it tries to reload the non existing Linux shared library. This can be reproduced on Windows as well if the Windows entries in the .gdextension are removed.\n\nRelates to #105615 as well since every time the error is printed the editor hangs for a few seconds.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCouldn't reproduce with an empty project and a simple GDExtension. I guess the reloading that happens scales with the project size.\nThe game that has the issue uses 5 GDExtensions and has quite a few heavy @tool scripts that could lead to the freeze.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nI can provide the source code if needed.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":